SUMMARY:Weaving Log Cabin on Rigid Heddle w/Peggy McIntosh\, Day 1
DESCRIPTION:Using a rigid heddle loom\, students will weave a scarf using a Log Cabin pattern. \nStudents will need a rigid heddle loom with a 7.5-dent or 8-dent heddle to fit the loom. \nLooms may be rented from the guild or the instructor on a first-come\, first-served basis but supplies are limited.  Contact the Guild Librarian\, or the instructor at plmcintosh@gmail.com\, to rent a loom. \n\n           Download QR
URL:https://bloomspinweave.org/event/weaving-log-cabin-on-rigid-heddle-w-peggy-mcintosh-day-1
LOCATION:Fiber Arts Center\, College Mall\, Bloomington\, 3038 East Third Street\, Bloomington\, IN\, 47401\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bloomington Spinners and Weavers Fiber Arts Guild Calendar
